  "key": "SFCC-149",
  "summary": "PDP UI — Notify Me Slide-out",
  "url": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/issue/18256",
  "description": "**As a** Shopper,\n\n**I want** to register for a back-in-stock notification from the PDP when my selected size is unavailable,\n\n**so that** I am alerted by email when my size is restocked and can return to purchase.\n\n----\n\nThis story covers the end-to-end Notify Me flow as experienced on the PDP: triggering the slide-out panel, submitting the registration form, and the post-submission confirmation state. Component build and accessibility implementation are covered in SFCC-741 (pdp/notify-me). The back-end email trigger and stock replenishment integration are out of scope — see SFCC-183 and SFCC-182.\n\n**Image for reference (Figma is leading):**\n\n![\"image-20260814-034042.png\"](image-20260814-034042.png)",
