{"result":"{
  "id": "18300",
  "key": "SFCC-183",
  "summary": "PDP – Notify Me: Back-in-Stock Email Trigger",
  "description": "**As a** Shopper,\n\n**I want** to receive an email notification when a size I registered for is back in stock,\n\n**so that** I can return to purchase before it sells out again.\n\n----\n\nWhen SFCC receives a stock replenishment signal from NewStore via MuleSoft, it evaluates the Notify Me subscription list for the restocked variant and sends the back-in-stock email to a configurable batch of subscribed customers (default: first 30). If the item remains in stock after a configurable time window, the next batch is notified, and so on until either the list is exhausted or the item sells out again. The email is sent from SFCC.\n\nThe stock replenishment signal integration (MuleSoft/NewStore) is a dependency but not in scope for this story. The Notify Me UI sign-up flow is covered in SFCC-149.",
